Git Configuration Levels

Git has three configuration levels.

System
   │
Global
   │
Local

Priority:

Local
   ↓
Global
   ↓
System

The Local configuration overrides the others.

1. System Configuration

Applies to every user on the machine.

View:

git config --system --list

Requires administrator privileges to modify.

2. Global Configuration

Applies to the current user.

Set username:

git config --global user.name "Anusha"

Set email:

git config --global user.email "anusha@example.com"

Verify:

git config --global --list
3. Local Configuration

Applies only to one repository.

git config --local user.name "ProjectUser"

Check:

git config --local --list
Check All Configuration
git config --list

Example:

user.name=Anusha
user.email=anusha@example.com
core.editor=code
init.defaultBranch=main
Useful Git Configuration

Set VS Code as default editor:

git config --global core.editor "code --wait"

Set default branch:

git config --global init.defaultBranch main

Enable colored output:

git config --global color.ui auto
