Key Takeaways
Git has System, Global, and Local configuration levels.
HTTPS authentication uses Personal Access Tokens instead of passwords.
SSH authentication uses a public/private key pair.
Never share your private SSH key.
Modern GitHub-to-Azure authentication should use OIDC instead of long-lived client secrets.